# Testing

Every meaningful feature should have appropriate tests.

Prioritize business logic, state transitions, data transformations, repository behavior, and critical UI behavior.

Use unit tests for business rules, calculations, validators, mappers, use cases, and state transitions.

Use widget tests for important user-visible behavior such as loading, empty, error, validation, interaction, and navigation.

Use integration tests for critical end-to-end flows.

Tests should verify behavior rather than implementation details.

Before finishing a change:
- Run relevant tests.
- Add tests for new business behavior.
- Update tests when behavior intentionally changes.
